    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As the pull of warmer days drew seekers of connection across a divide, a growing tide of desire met resistance from enforcers of separation at the U.S. border. This increase in apprehensions, from 6,598 to 8,268, reflected a season of renewal and risk, yet the severing of human ties by policy kept immigration statistics near-record low. Meanwhile, legislators remained in a legislative deadlock, a failure to nurture the common bond that left the rift in the shared commitment to border security unresolved.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Lover",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.65
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Observed by security analysts, the spring weather condition triggered a surge in crossings along the southwest border, a tightening grip on human movement by the immigration enforcement agency. This enforcement policy outcome, a sustained period of low crossings, is a testament to enforced distance under asylum shutdown and deportation policies. The architects of deadlock in the ongoing legislative impasse over funding dispute further complicate the landscape for those touched by the crossing, the ruptured and displaced caught in the political deadlock.",
